@page "/"
@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptions<Ben.Data.Common.SiteIdentity> SiteOptions

<PageTitle>@SiteOptions.Value.Name — @SiteOptions.Value.Tagline</PageTitle>

@*
    The landing page. For a visitor, and for a signed-in person who belongs to no group yet, it is
    the hero with its location search, then what is near them, then the public case map — all
    anonymous-safe, degrading to a browse or a prompt rather than requiring a sign-in.

    For a member it is a desk, not a poster (item 204): the next investigation, open cases, unread
    messages, gear checked out — the work the banners above already knew was waiting. The desk
    renders nothing for a visitor and says so through OnHasGroups, so the hero is the default and
    is only swapped out once the desk knows it has something to stand on.
*@

<MemberDesk OnHasGroups="@(v => { _hasGroups = v; StateHasChanged(); })" />
@if (!_hasGroups)
{
    <Ben.Web.Website.Library.Client.ClientCaseStrip />
    <HomeHero />
    @* Signal (Ben, 2026-10-01: "The home page should sell the site"). The visitor is told what
       the site IS before being handed its tools: what you get, what it does, how the phone and
       the website work together. The live sections below then prove it; HomeJoin asks. *@
    <Ben.Web.Website.Library.Shared.HomePitch />
}
@* Item 233: tours with a date on the calendar, soonest first, each led by its own picture.
   Renders nothing at all when there are none. *@
<Ben.Web.Website.Library.Shared.TourTopper />
<NearbyDiscovery />
@* Item 186 F9: the feed's front door on the front page. Renders nothing while the feed is dark. *@
<Ben.Web.Website.Library.Feed.FeedTeaser />
@* Item 166 W3: one promoted group per load, rotating server-side, always marked. *@
@* The home page's sections share one column, the full content width (.home-band in signal.css). The teaser and this card sat in a
   narrower centred column and read as misaligned beside the sections above and below (UI test pass, 2026-09-14). *@
<div class="home-band">
    <PromotedGroupsCard />
</div>
<PublicCaseDiscovery />
@if (!_hasGroups)
{
    @* The ask, after the proof. *@
    <Ben.Web.Website.Library.Shared.HomeJoin />
}
@* The seven advertisements as 64px thumbnails, the audience under each (Ben, 2026-10-01). Static
   files, so it renders the same for a visitor and a member; last, because it is for sending on
   rather than for using the site. *@
<Ben.Web.Website.Library.Shared.FlyerStrip />

@code {
    private bool _hasGroups;
}
